   AlphaServer GS80, GS160, GS320 class and the AlphaServer ES47, ES80 and 
GS1280 class boxes both provide non-uniform memory access.  The latter series 
scales rather better -- more processors, without incurring unnecessary latency 
-- due to the toroidal system interconnect design.  And if you're watching 
carefully at the very lowest levels, you can see differences between local and 
remote memory accesses.

   There are a handful of criteria for OpenVMS SMP support, and IIRC these are 
listed in the IDSM books.

   Within OpenVMS, see the RAD mechanisms.


