I don't think the VAX situation was much more different than the PDP.
The only disk systems not supported on the VAX were RP02/RP03/RPR02
and the RK05... all of which were very obsolete by then.  There was an
RK11/RK05 driver set in DECUS... so you could get them running on the
VAX.

I'm not sure if there ever were any RP04's on VAX systems -- but I
couldn't see why not since the registers were the same as RP05/RP06
drives... just the density/cyl count was different.

The RK06/7 RL01/RL02/RX02 subsystems were available and supported IIRC.
The RM80 and RA80/81/82 and such were as well.

And there could be multiple Unibus subsystems on the VAX -- so you could
really get more stuff than on the 11's.  The VAX, however usually had
it's storage on Massbus devices until the UDA50 and CI came out.

VAX configurations were interesting because the bus loads and Unibus
configs could be worked out by that AI program -- down to what cards
went in what slots...  That wasn't around for the 11's... which required
the Field Service and District Support grunts to figure bus reflections
and loads by hand.

Bill



