>the command 

>   SYSGEN> AUTOCONFIGURE ALL

>I've done this many times in the past with no problem.  Now, it froze
>the process doing it, caused members of shadow sets served by that node
>to be dismounted (after throwing the whole shadow sets into mount
>verification for a while first) and put a single disk (a CD in the
>internal CD drive) into permanent mount verification. 

VMS only supports certain configurations for "hotswapping".  The reason,
as you found out, is it doesn't always work.  The AUTOCONFIG may put
devices into states the drivers don't expect.

In the future, you may try to configure only the specific drive.
AUTOCONFIGURE /SELECT=DKB300 or whatever, to configure that specific
drive (only).  Even then, you may  put the SCSI bus driver into a
funky state, but it should be OK.  Wildcards work (/SEL=DKB*).


