Sure -- it's easy when the hardware's limited to under 10 slots.
Plug it in.

Imagine a PCI bus running 48+ slots... per chassis.
With three foot bus jumpers running between the rack mounted cabinets.

There are times when I'd kill for something with as many slots as a
PDP11 or a VAX.  The problem is the passive backplane stuff can have
similar restrictions and reflections.

Plug and Play worked pretty well in the VAX... you plugged the card in
and it worked.  Autogen is your friend.

However when it got flaky the AI program could analyze the bus and fix
the problem by moving cards around.



