But it used critical section locking last I looked, so would scale
very badly. IMO common memory systems are better than bus based SMP
systems iff you can sync caches with small overhead.

> I guess I'll have to buckle down and study some of the DEC operating
> systems some day.

> Has the code been released for any version of any of them?

Look on Tim Shoppa's site, trailing-edge.com. He has Tops-10 and
Twenex, but I don't thing the sources for that have been fully
recovered as yet.

