The REL file was copied into the TOPS10.REL file which was then
used to produce the monitor.EXE file.  One could say that 
CPNSER was the "device" driver for SMP.  Note that SMP allowed
any CPU to do I/O to any device that was physically connected
to that CPU.  I don't think this thread noticed this.
People tend to confuse parallel processing with our definition
of SMP.

