>How do the build scripts work?  Are there any? 

Read any MIGnnn documentation, where nnn=the monitor version
number.  It will step you through the MONGEN dialog.  This is
the program that outputs the MAC source files that set
the values for all the macros that generate device structures,
monitor tables, etc. and are input to the assemblies of
COMMON.MAC, COMMOD.MAC and COMDEV.MAC.  These create the
site-specific REL files that have to do with all hardware
and software configurations.  

> Is the build process 
>semimanual?

Huh?  Oh.  manual...I read annual.  Yes.  This had to be so because
every customer had different hardware and software configuration
requirements.  
>
>I ask because I won't really learn anything about TOPS-10 and SMP until 
>I can modify it and see the result in an emulator.

